{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "217c755b-2fc0-822d-8adf-7211c2d804e2",
  "created_at": "2026-01-29T13:10:56-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Adriana Herrera",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Kevin Sousa",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-29T13:07:32-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works, this is Kevin."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-29T13:07:35-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hello, Kevin. Yes, um, this is Adriana Herrera. I think I'm calling about a storm drain, maybe the right department? On my street."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-29T13:07:45-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yep, that's us. Storm drains are Public Works. What's going on with it?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-29T13:07:51-05:00",
      "duration": 18,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Well, it's sort of backed up, I think, whenever it rains hard. After the storm Sunday and Monday, the snow that turned to rain, the whole street flooded. Again. And that was three days ago and I think there's still a puddle at the corner."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-29T13:08:09-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, so the drain's clogged up and the street's holding water. What's the address?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-29T13:08:15-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "211 Dixon Street. In the North End, maybe four houses up from the corner."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-29T13:08:21-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "211 Dixon, North End. Got it. How deep did the water get, would you say?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-29T13:08:28-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I think it came up to about the hubcaps, sort of. On the cars parked along the curb. My neighbor's car, anyway, I think it was up to the hubcaps."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-29T13:08:41-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Wow, okay. Hubcap deep on Dixon. Did it get into your house at all?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-29T13:08:47-05:00",
      "duration": 19,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, no, not this time. Thank goodness. But I remember the basement flooded back in 2018, maybe the fall of that year, and nothing like that since. So the street flooding again, that's what I'm upset about. It keeps going and nobody comes to clean that drain."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-29T13:09:06-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Understood. So the basement was 2018, nothing since, but the street flooded this time. I'm writing that down. Has anyone been out to look at the drain, that you know of?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-29T13:09:19-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I don't think so. Maybe somebody did and I missed it, but I don't think anyone has. I'd like the drain cleaned out, please. That's really what I'm asking. Before the next storm."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-29T13:09:33-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, that's reasonable. I'll put in a request for a crew to inspect and clean the catch basin at 211 Dixon. Is the grate itself blocked, like leaves or ice, or can you tell?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-29T13:09:47-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I think it's sort of packed with leaves and maybe some ice and gravel from the plows. I couldn't say for sure. I didn't want to go poking at it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-29T13:10:00-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, good, leave it be. Crews are pretty stacked after a storm like this, but this goes on the list. Can I get a number in case they need to reach you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-29T13:10:13-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Of course. It's 401-555-0156. That's the landline."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-29T13:10:17-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Four-oh-one, five-five-five, oh-one-five-six. Perfect."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-29T13:10:20-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You know, my dad taught me to handle things like this by phone. Call, give the address, be polite, and call again if they don't come. So I'll call again, I think, if I need to."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-29T13:10:35-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Ha, your dad had it right. Call back anytime and just mention the Dixon Street drain, and we'll pull up the request."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-29T13:10:44-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thank you, Kevin. I do appreciate it. I just hope it gets done soon."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-29T13:10:50-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "We'll get it moving. Take care, Ms. Herrera."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-29T13:10:54-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You too. Goodbye."
    }
  ],
